  "required_walking_policy_id": "r10j_v50_settled_hold_route_v1",
  "rationale": "R10J campaign v1 uses the same production launcher, worker, native adapter, complete capture, cold replay, finite evaluator and publication for a fresh seed-40200 pair and, only after the separate committed authority, six held-out cells. Only seed and role select the preregistered prefix fixture; no controller, DLL, task threshold, ramp/hold budget, walking arithmetic or stop change. The original v1 launcher refusal remains unchanged. The repaired production route must pass a fresh complete pair before freeze; component replay does not substitute for that prerequisite.",
  "predecessor_contract": "sdk/recovery/r10j_v50_walking_entry_contract_v5.json",
  "allowed_evaluation_segments": [
    "walking_resume",
    "matched_continuation"
  ],
  "predecessor_contract_sha256": "sha256:d7bee6db97617b0b8a0ceab5f9c8c1eff294fa6c629c73af11f490c89f8793a6",
  "integration_revision": "Campaign v4 preserves the v3 partial zero-world gate stopped at 79 checks before any physical claim. Cold header review found the smoke report lacks top-level seed_label and seed_sha256 required by the next original campaign reader predicate. Publish both fields from the validated seed identity. Extract the existing complete campaign retention predicates unchanged and exercise that actual validator against native emitted headers and missing-field controls. Preserve the prior physical invalid pair, strict comparisons, controller, DLL, task criteria, ramp/hold budgets, and unobserved six-cell population."
